WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.516
A security control is a safeguard or countermeasure designed to reduce risk.

00:00:05.516 --> 00:00:09.126
Controls can be technical, operational, managerial, or privacy-focused.

00:00:09.126 --> 00:00:13.188
Technical controls may include access control mechanisms, logging, encryption,

00:00:13.188 --> 00:00:15.444
network protections, and system hardening.

00:00:15.444 --> 00:00:19.506
Operational controls may include incident response procedures, training programs,

00:00:19.506 --> 00:00:20.860
and account reviews.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.470
Managerial controls support governance, planning, risk assessment, authorization,

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:25.373
and oversight.

00:00:25.373 --> 00:00:29.435
Together, these controls help organizations protect systems, detect problems,

00:00:29.435 --> 00:00:32.594
respond to incidents, and recover from disruptions.

00:00:32.594 --> 00:00:35.753
A control is more than a label.

00:00:35.753 --> 00:00:38.461
It needs ownership, implementation, evidence, assessment,

00:00:38.461 --> 00:00:41.620
and maintenance to be useful in practice.
